"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,229\nThe Learning Brain. Series 3: Generative AI\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,314\nEpisode 9\n\n3\n00:00:07,394 --> 00:00:09,472\nWriting is thinking\n\n4\n00:00:12,272 --> 00:00:16,917\nFifty four students wrote short essays over four months,\n\n5\n00:00:17,221 --> 00:00:18,829\nin three groups: with ChatGPT,\n\n6\n00:00:18,829 --> 00:00:20,030\nwith a search engine,\n\n7\n00:00:20,205 --> 00:00:22,355\nor with only their own heads.\n\n8\n00:00:22,767 --> 00:00:26,093\nElectrodes recorded their brain activity as they wrote.\n\n9\n00:00:26,263 --> 00:00:30,451\nBrain connectivity scaled down with the amount of outside support.\n\n10\n00:00:30,925 --> 00:00:33,249\nThe unaided group showed the strongest,\n\n11\n00:00:33,269 --> 00:00:34,898\nmost widespread networks.\n\n12\n00:00:35,239 --> 00:00:37,246\nSearch users were in between.\n\n13\n00:00:37,645 --> 00:00:39,856\nThe AI group showed the weakest.\n\n14\n00:00:40,026 --> 00:00:46,757\nMinutes after finishing, most of the AI group could not correctly quote a sentence from the essay they had just written.\n\n15\n00:00:47,270 --> 00:00:51,536\nIn the first session the reported figure was about eighty three percent,\n\n16\n00:00:51,921 --> 00:00:54,863\nagainst about eleven percent in the other groups.\n\n17\n00:00:55,278 --> 00:00:58,356\nThey also felt the least ownership of their essays.\n\n18\n00:00:58,526 --> 00:00:59,729\nIn a fourth session,\n\n19\n00:00:59,755 --> 00:01:00,869\nthe groups swapped.\n\n20\n00:01:01,277 --> 00:01:03,447\nStudents who had first written unaided,\n\n21\n00:01:03,502 --> 00:01:05,196\nand then used AI,\n\n22\n00:01:05,390 --> 00:01:08,979\nshowed higher engagement and used it more strategically.\n\n23\n00:01:09,490 --> 00:01:15,384\nStudents moving the other way showed weaker connectivity than those who had practised unaided all along.\n\n24\n00:01:15,554 --> 00:01:17,906\nThis is the generation effect again.\n\n25\n00:01:18,302 --> 00:01:21,040\nWriting is not only a way to show thinking.\n\n26\n00:01:21,344 --> 00:01:23,395\nIt is where much of the thinking happens.\n\n27\n00:01:23,667 --> 00:01:26,256\nHand it off, and the encoding goes with it.\n\n28\n00:01:26,426 --> 00:01:27,225\nA caution.\n\n29\n00:01:27,657 --> 00:01:29,863\nThis is a preprint with a small sample: fifty four people,\n\n30\n00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:33,499\nand only eighteen in the swap session.\n\n31\n00:01:33,974 --> 00:01:36,793\nEEG connectivity is an indirect measure.\n\n32\n00:01:37,145 --> 00:01:38,776\nTreat it as a warning sign,\n\n33\n00:01:38,796 --> 00:01:39,800\nnot a verdict.\n\n34\n00:01:39,970 --> 00:01:40,762\nFor teaching.\n\n35\n00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:47,552\nProtect an unaided stage: have students draft their ideas and structure before any AI use.\n\n36\n00:01:47,944 --> 00:01:51,524\nAsk them to explain or quote their own work afterwards.\n\n37\n00:01:51,846 --> 00:01:53,526\nAnd when AI comes in,\n\n38\n00:01:53,722 --> 00:01:57,793\nuse it to critique and extend a draft the student already owns.\n\n39\n00:01:57,963 --> 00:01:59,942\nWriting is thinking made visible.\n\n40\n00:02:00,279 --> 00:02:02,054\nIf AI does the writing,\n\n41\n00:02:02,108 --> 00:02:03,694\nthe thinking may never happen.\n\n"
